; Source: HSPICE Reference Manual: Commands and Control Options, D-2010.12,
; chapter 4 "Digital Vector File Commands", the "Examples" of TRISE, TFALL,
; VIH, VIL, VOH, VOL, VTH, OUT or OUTZ, and TRIZ, in that order. Their masks
; describe fifteen vectors, three 1-bit, then one each of 1, 2, 3 and 4 bits,
; then eight 1-bit; the RADIX and VNAME lines are added to declare them.
RADIX 1 1 1 1234 11111111
VNAME V1 V2 V3 V4 V5[[1:0]] V6[[2:0]] V7[[3:0]] V8 V9 V10 V11 V12 V13 V14 V15
; TRISE: 0.3 for all; 0.5 for vectors 2 to 7; 0.8 for vectors 8 to 11
TRISE 0.3
TRISE 0.5 0 1 1 137F 00000000
TRISE 0.8 0 0 0 0000 11110000
; TFALL: 0.5 for all; 0.3 for vectors 2 to 7; 0.9 for vectors 8 to 11
TFALL 0.5
TFALL 0.3 0 1 1 137F 00000000
TFALL 0.9 0 0 0 0000 11110000
; VIH: 5 V for all; 3.5 V for the last eight
VIH 5.0
VIH 3.5 0 0 0 0000 11111111
; VIL: 0 V for all; 0.5 V for the last eight
VIL 0.0
VIL 0.5 0 0 0 0000 11111111
; VOH: 4.5 V for the first seven; 3.5 V for the last eight
VOH 4.75
VOH 4.5 1 1 1 137F 00000000
VOH 3.5 0 0 0 0000 11111111
; VOL: 0.5 V for the first three; 0.2 V for vectors 4 to 7; 0 V for the rest
VOL 0.0
VOL 0.2 0 0 0 137F 00000000
VOL 0.5 1 1 1 0000 00000000
; VTH: 2.5 V for the first seven; 1.75 V for the last eight
VTH 1.75
VTH 2.5 1 1 1 137F 00000000
VTH 1.75 0 0 0 0000 11111111
; OUT/OUTZ: 15.1 ohm for all; 150 ohm for vectors 1 to 3; 50.5 ohm for 4 to 7
OUT 15.1
OUT 150 1 1 1 0000 00000000
OUTZ 50.5 0 0 0 137F 00000000
; TRIZ: 15.1 Mohm for all; 150 Mohm for vectors 1 to 3; 50.5 Mohm for 4 to 7
TRIZ 15.1Meg
TRIZ 150Meg 1 1 1 0000 00000000
TRIZ 50.5Meg 0 0 0 137F 00000000
